text.section:
The Board may issue a restricted volunteer license to a dentist who:

Held an unrestricted license in Virginia or another state as a licensee in good standing at the time the license expired or became inactive;


Is volunteering for a public health or community free clinic that provides dental services to populations of underserved people;


Has fulfilled the Board's requirement related to knowledge of the laws and regulations governing the practice of dentistry in Virginia;


Has not failed a clinical examination within the past five years; and


Has had at least five years of clinical practice.

A person holding a restricted volunteer license under this section shall:

Only practice in public health or community free clinics that provide dental services to underserved populations;


Only treat patients who have been screened by the approved clinic and are eligible for treatment;


Attest on a form provided by the Board that he will not receive remuneration directly or indirectly for providing dental services; and


Not be required to complete continuing education in order to renew such a license.
